{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:47:06.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3s4jwl+pm-8patuh+pm-g2zzus+pm-gh1769+pm-lulgxc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T08:47:06.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Measured 2026-11-23 on the 2026.11.23 build. A project extension registering item fields full, limit and json leaves pm list --full (projection mode full), pm list --limit 2 (count 2, applied_limit 2) and pm search --full working as before; extension fields are set through the repeatable --field name=value assignment, not a per-field option, so no CLI option is shadowed and the add-field collision check does not apply. pm list --fields full and pm get <id> --fields full read the value. The one overlap is the projection-mode vocabulary of --output-include: pm get <id> --output-include full,limit reads full as the full projection mode and refuses projection_options_mutually_exclusive, so such a field is selected with --fields. docs/EXTENSIONS.md now states both.\n\nScope addition delivered: mutateWorkspaceSettings (src/sdk/extension-command-context.ts) runs assertFieldDefinitionOptionsAvailable on every inline schema field definition the callback adds or changes, dry run included, before anything is written; a definition left exactly as stored is not judged, so an unrelated write keeps a legacy definition (validate keeps reporting it). Spec: tests/unit/sdk/transactions/settings-field-admission.spec.ts.\n\nSide finding filed as pm-dhlij3: an extension field named priority (reserved) activates and then makes every create and update exit 2 with command_failed, and package doctor names only the MCP collision.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:47:06.302Z"}],"before_hash":"2284ec047f0c786c0168ee99e4a9d52896767bf38b441ba5f5df742047d588cc","after_hash":"6c8d01671d8cfbe21a5cac902a87b9bcdaa96a895fd83a598b5cc89e8e382237","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"873eaf6c80448e2b55f2ccbc70b7c797152ad66b6c9bb841829f13d76cca8e5d"}
